 excess kurtosis k4/k2^2 > 0 => LEPTOKURTIC/bimodal = double-well phi^4 (b<0) = max extreme-mass = gK8 extremizer.

================================================================================================
 THE phi^4 CAP SPLIT: cap_k = C(k+1,2)/91 (quadratic) - dip_k (quartic stabilizer)
================================================================================================
  k |        cap_k | C(k+1,2)/91 (b, quadratic) | dip_k (lambda, quartic) | quartic active?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  8 |    2243/5880 |                36/91 |             1081/76440 | ACTIVE (binding)
  9 |    1979/4004 |                45/91 |                 1/4004 | ACTIVE (binding)
 10 |        55/91 |                55/91 |                      0 | off (pure quadratic)
 11 |        66/91 |                66/91 |                      0 | off (pure quadratic)
 12 |          6/7 |                  6/7 |                      0 | off (pure quadratic)
 13 |            1 |                    1 |                      0 | off (pure quadratic)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 The gK8 dual L_yK8 = 10 - 10 S1 + 10 S2 - 9 S3 + 6 S4: the +6 S4 QUARTIC term is nonzero only at the
 k=8 binding row; k=9,10 duals stop at S3, k>=11 at S2. So the QUARTIC stabilizer S4 activates EXACTLY
 where the cap dips below the quadratic pair-Pascal -- the phi^4 structure exp(-lambda S^4 - b S^2).

================================================================================================
 PROOF-RELEVANT READING
================================================================================================
 cap-extremality's only non-pairwise content (S63/S64) = the dip at k=8,9 = the QUARTIC term S4.
 phi^4/Lee-Yang says the quartic STABILIZES (lambda>0 => bounded correction, right sign), and the
 double-well (b<0, k4>0) is the bimodal extreme-mass that IS the gK8 extremizer. So 'bound the dip'
 (the open obligation) = 'bound the quartic cumulant S4', a SINGLE 4th-moment bound with a guaranteed
 sign -- the phi^4 reframe of coverage extremality.
